---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  lang="en"
  description={`${site.name} privacy policy: what data leaves your device, why, and for how long.`}
  alternate="/confidentialite"
>
  <article class="container prose page">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: {site.privacyUpdated.en}</p>

    <div class="summary">
      <p><strong>In short</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>No account, no ads, no analytics, no tracking.</li>
        <li>Games, players and history stay on your device and in your iCloud.</li>
        <li>
          Three optional features go through a server, only for as long as needed: live sharing,
          the score on the Lock Screen, and shared profiles.
        </li>
        <li>No data is sold or used for advertising.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is published by {site.publisher}. For any question about your data:
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Games, rounds, players, their avatars and your history are stored on the device. If iCloud is
      turned on, they also sync to your private iCloud database, managed by Apple, across your own
      devices. The publisher has no access to it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The camera is only used to scan a QR code (to join a game or link a profile). No image is
      saved or sent.
    </p>

    <h2>What leaves your device, and why</h2>
    <p>
      The three features below use Supabase (database and real-time messaging hosting, region:
      {site.supabaseRegion.en}). They only run if you use them.
    </p>

    <h3>Live game sharing</h3>
    <p>
      While a game is shared, the server keeps: the six-digit pairing code, a random session
      identifier, the game identifier, which game is played, the number of players, the generic
      device name (for example “iPhone”) and its platform. This lets other devices find the game
      from the code.
    </p>
    <p>
      The game content (nicknames, scores, rounds) travels between devices
      <strong>end-to-end encrypted</strong>, with a key derived from the pairing code. It is not
      stored, and the server cannot read it.
    </p>

    <h3>Score on the Lock Screen (Live Activity)</h3>
    <p>
      To update the Lock Screen and the Dynamic Island while the app is in the background, the
      server keeps the notification token provided by Apple, a random device identifier created by
      the app, and the latest standings shown (nicknames and scores of the top four). The update is
      delivered by Apple’s notification service. You can turn this off in Settings › {site.name} ›
      Live Activities.
    </p>

    <h3>Shared profiles</h3>
    <p>
      When you link a player’s profile with a friend (by QR code), a summary of each finished game
      they took part in (nickname, simple avatar, rank and score of each player) is left on the
      server for their device, which picks it up the next time they open the app.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Deleted</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Live shared game</td>
            <td>When sharing stops, and at most 24 hours after it started</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Lock Screen</td>
            <td>At most 30 minutes after the last round</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Shared profile summary</td>
            <td>As soon as it is picked up, and at most after 30 days</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Data on the device and in iCloud</td>
            <td>When you delete it, or by deleting the app and its iCloud data</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Legal basis</h2>
    <p>
      Data sent to the server is processed only to provide the feature you chose to use (GDPR
      Article 6(1)(b)). It is never tied to an identity: the app has no accounts.
    </p>

    <h2>Recipients</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Supabase, to host the temporary data described above.</li>
      <li>Apple, for iCloud and to deliver Lock Screen updates.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No other third party receives any data.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access, correct, erase and object. Since the app has no accounts, server
      data is not tied to your identity and deletes itself within the periods above. For any
      request: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. You may also lodge a complaint
      with your data protection authority (in France, the <a href="https://www.cnil.fr">CNIL</a>).
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The app asks for no personal information and is suitable for all ages. No data is
      specifically collected from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>Any change to this policy is published on this page, with its update date.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl);
  }
</style>
